{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b73b-6f0a-7cc5-b1d3-796ef79a0189","session_id":"01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_01_r6rHOARZf7dv0SLSX7Z09085","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→const DEFAULT_FAIL_MESSAGE = 'stub register failed'\n   2→\n   3→export function createHostStub({ failPaths = [], failInject = false, failMessage = DEFAULT_FAIL_MESSAGE } = {}) {\n   4→  const registered = []\n   5→  const effects = []\n   6→  const injectCalls = []\n   7→  const handlers = new Map()\n   8→\n   9→  const httpCtx = {\n  10→    effect(fn, name) {\n  11→      effects.push(name)\n  12→      return fn()\n  13→    },\n  14→    webServer: {\n  15→      register(registration) {\n  16→        if (!registration || typeof registration !== 'object') throw new TypeError('registration must be an object')\n  17→        if (registration.kind !== 'exact') throw new TypeError(`registration kind must be exact, got ${String(registration.kind)}`)\n  18→        if (typeof registration.path !== 'string' || !registration.path.startsWith('/')) throw new TypeError(`registration path must start with /, got ${String(registration.path)}`)\n  19→        if (typeof registration.handler !== 'function') throw new TypeError('registration handler must be a function')\n  20→        if (failPaths.includes('*') || failPaths.includes(registration.path)) throw new Error(`${failMessage}: ${registration.path}`)\n  21→        registered.push({ kind: registration.kind, path: registration.path })\n  22→        handlers.set(registration.path, registration.handler)\n  23→        return undefined\n  24→      },\n  25→    },\n  26→  }\n  27→\n  28→  const ctx = {\n  29→    inject(services, callback) {\n  30→      injectCalls.push(services)\n  31→      if (failInject) throw new Error('stub inject failed')\n  32→      return callback(httpCtx)\n  33→    },\n  34→  }\n  35→\n  36→  function handlerFor(routePath) {\n  37→    const handler = handlers.get(routePath)\n  38→    if (!handler) throw new Error(`no handler registered for ${routePath}`)\n  39→    return handler\n  40→  }\n  41→\n  42→  async function request(routePath, options = {}) {\n  43→    const {\n  44→      method = 'GET',\n  45→      url = routePath,\n  46→      headers = {},\n  47→      remoteAddress = '127.0.0.1',\n  48→      host = 'localhost',\n  49→      origin,\n  50→      body,\n  51→    } = options\n  52→\n  53→    const handler = handlerFor(routePath)\n  54→    const listeners = new Map()\n  55→    const reqHeaders = { ...headers, host }\n  56→    if (origin !== undefined) reqHeaders.origin = origin\n  57→\n  58→    const req = {\n  59→      method,\n  60→      url,\n  61→      headers: reqHeaders,\n  62→      socket: { remoteAddress },\n  63→      on(event, fn) {\n  64→        const list = listeners.get(event) || []\n  65→        list.push(fn)\n  66→        listeners.set(event, list)\n  67→        return req\n  68→      },\n  69→      destroy() {},\n  70→    }\n  71→\n  72→    const out = { statusCode: 200, headers: {}, body: '' }\n  73→    let finish = () => {}\n  74→    const done = new Promise((resolve) => { finish = resolve })\n  75→\n  76→    const res = {\n  77→      get statusCode() { return out.statusCode },\n  78→      set statusCode(value) { out.statusCode = value },\n  79→      setHeader(key, value) { out.headers[String(key).toLowerCase()] = value },\n  80→      end(chunk) {\n  81→        out.body = chunk === undefined ? '' : String(chunk)\n  82→        finish()\n  83→      },\n  84→    }\n  85→\n  86→    const result = handler(req, res)\n  87→    await Promise.resolve()\n  88→\n  89→    const payload = body === undefined ? '' : (typeof body === 'string' ? body : JSON.stringify(body))\n  90→    if (payload !== '') for (const fn of listeners.get('data') || []) fn(Buffer.from(payload))\n  91→    for (const fn of listeners.get('end') || []) fn()\n  92→\n  93→    await done\n  94→    if (result && typeof result.then === 'function') await result\n  95→\n  96→    return { statusCode: out.statusCode, headers: out.headers, body: out.body }\n  97→  }\n  98→\n  99→  return { ctx, registered, effects, injectCalls, handlerFor, request }\n 100→}\n 101→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","_messageId":"01a1b73b678a754ba710c889b8f03e9e","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b73b678a754ba710c889b8f03e9e","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b73b678a754ba710c889b8f03e9e","traceparent":"00-74b9dfff07cab8a4abe921b11db84963-aa0f475921555b00-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:18:08.010Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b73b-6ee1-74d0-bfa8-46bf98468ae7","session_id":"01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd","message":{"id":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Compare with design §8.3 for host stub:\n- `ctx.inject(services, cb)`: record, failInject throws, else synchronous cb. ✓\n- `httpCtx.effect(fn, name)`: record name, call fn synchronously, return result, propagate. ✓\n- register validation ✓, failPaths incl '*' ✓, records `{kind, path}` ✓.\n- `request(path, {...})` constructs req with socket.remoteAddress, headers host/origin, body via on data/end; res with statusCode/setHeader/end; calls handler and awaits; returns {statusCode, headers, body}. ✓\n- returns `{ ctx, registered, effects, injectCalls, handlerFor(path), request(path, opts) }` ✓\n\nOne issue: request resolves `done` only when res.end is called. If handler never ends, hangs. Fine.\n\nOld cli: note old `usage record` fails if JSON parse of undefined → error \"bad --json: Unexpected token...\" Actually JSON.parse(undefined) throws \"Unexpected token u in JSON at position 0\". Same behavior preserved.\n\nOld behavior: unknown command still loaded config first. New: route first. Per design, that's intended.\n\nOld: `fail` used process.exit. New returns exitCode.\n\nNow check the design detail in §5.1: \"解析不到则写 stderr `ERROR: usage...`\". Implemented.\n\nOne deviation: design §5.1 says for `models` subcommand missing or 'list' → models/list. Implementation: `if (sub === '' || sub === 'list') sub = null`. So `models ''`→list. Design said \"缺省或为 list\". Fine.\n\nNow `lib/index.js`: compare to design §6 carefully.\n\n- `createPlugin(hostCtx, settings = {}, deps = {})` returns `{registered, errors}`. ✓\n- `getRegistration()` returns copy of last report; status failed if errors non-empty; if never called returns placeholder. ✓\n- `apply` — strict throws. ✓\n- deps.ctx default createContext(). ✓\n- settings: configPath default ctx.env.CLIWORKER_CONFIG or defaultHome(config.json) ✓; readonly default false — hmm, `readonly` isn't really used in implementation. Design says `settings` 取 `configPath`, `readonly`（缺省 false）、`strict`（缺省 false）. It doesn't say what readonly does. The old index.js probably didn't have readonly either. Let me check the old index.js at HEAD to compare.\n\nLet me read main repo's lib/index.js.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","_messageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b73b-6ee1-74d0-bfa8-46bf98468ae7","traceparent":"00-74b9dfff07cab8a4abe921b11db84963-aa0f475921555b00-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:18:13.241Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b73b-8379-73b8-9b08-0fea87ac1d32","session_id":"01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd","message":{"id":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_9TQy2tm6PjXIorAmw8v88836","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\lib\\index.js"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":90882,"output_tokens":607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":88576,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","_messageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","traceparent":"00-74b9dfff07cab8a4abe921b11db84963-aa0f475921555b00-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:18:13.241Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b73b-8390-7c6b-8d21-fd20f490f4cf","session_id":"01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_9TQy2tm6PjXIorAmw8v88836","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→/**\n   2→ * dsh-cliworker — DSH host plugin.\n   3→ *\n   4→ * AgentLine and other clients only need the model source pointer:\n   5→ *   modelSource = { kind: \"cliworker\", command: \"node\",\n   6→ *                   args: [\".../dsh-CLIWorker/bin/cliworker.mjs\", \"--config\", \"...\"] }\n   7→ *\n   8→ * The plugin exposes the same selection contract over DSH routes for UI use.\n   9→ */\n  10→import path from 'node:path'\n  11→import os from 'node:os'\n  12→import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n  13→import { loadConfig } from '../lib/config.mjs'\n  14→import { providerStatus } from '../lib/availability.mjs'\n  15→import { listModels, selectModels } from '../lib/select.mjs'\n  16→import { forecast } from '../lib/forecast.mjs'\n  17→\n  18→const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url))\n  19→const DEFAULTS = {\n  20→  configPath: process.env.CLIWORKER_CONFIG || path.join(process.env.CLIWORKER_HOME || path.join(os.homedir(), '.cliworker'), 'config.json'),\n  21→  readonly: false,\n  22→}\n  23→\n  24→function send(res, body, code = 200) {\n  25→  res.statusCode = code\n  26→  res.setHeader('content-type', 'application/json; charset=utf-8')\n  27→  res.setHeader('cache-control', 'no-store')\n  28→  res.end(JSON.stringify(body))\n  29→}\n  30→\n  31→function readBody(req) {\n  32→  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n  33→    let raw = ''\n  34→    req.on('data', (d) => { raw += d.toString(); if (raw.length > 2_000_000) req.destroy() })\n  35→    req.on('end', () => { try { resolve(raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : {}) } catch (e) { reject(e) } })\n  36→    req.on('error', reject)\n  37→  })\n  38→}\n  39→\n  40→export const name = 'cliworker'\n  41→\n  42→export function apply(ctx, config = {}) {\n  43→  const settings = { ...DEFAULTS, ...(config || {}) }\n  44→  const getConfig = () => loadConfig({ file: settings.configPath })\n  45→\n  46→  try {\n  47→    ctx.inject(['webServer'], (httpCtx) => {\n  48→      const route = (p, name, handler) => httpCtx.effect(() => httpCtx.webServer.register({ kind: 'exact', path: p, handler }), name)\n  49→\n  50→      route('/cliworker/providers', 'cliworker: providers', async (_req, res) => {\n  51→        try { const c = getConfig(); send(res, { ok: true, providers: providerStatus(c) }) } catch (e) { send(res, { ok: false, error: String(e.message || e) }, 500) }\n  52→      })\n  53→      route('/cliworker/models', 'cliworker: models', async (_req, res) => {\n  54→        try { const c = getConfig(); send(res, { ok: true, models: listModels(c, { status: providerStatus(c), includeDeprecated: false }) }) } catch (e) { send(res, { ok: false, error: String(e.message || e) }, 500) }\n  55→      })\n  56→      route('/cliworker/select', 'cliworker: select', async (req, res) => {\n  57→        try {\n  58→          const c = getConfig()\n  59→          const body = req.method === 'GET' ? { request: JSON.parse(new URL(req.url || '/', 'http://local').searchParams.get('request') || '{}') } : await readBody(req)\n  60→          const request = body.request || body\n  61→          send(res, { ok: true, ...selectModels(c, request, { status: providerStatus(c) }) })\n  62→        } catch (e) { send(res, { ok: false, error: String(e.message || e) }, 400) }\n  63→      })\n  64→      route('/cliworker/forecast', 'cliworker: forecast', async (req, res) => {\n  65→        try {\n  66→          const c = getConfig()\n  67→          const model = new URL(req.url || '/', 'http://local').searchParams.get('model')\n  68→          send(res, { ok: true, forecast: forecast({ model, prices: model ? c.models[model]?.prices : undefined, quota: model ? c.quotas?.[c.models[model]?.provider] : null }) })\n  69→        } catch (e) { send(res, { ok: false, error: String(e.message || e) }, 500) }\n  70→      })\n  71→    })\n  72→  } catch (e) {\n  73→    console.error('[cliworker] webServer inject failed:', e.message)\n  74→  }\n  75→}\n  76→\n  77→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","_messageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b73b6ee174d0bfa846bd2100bb35","traceparent":"00-74b9dfff07cab8a4abe921b11db84963-aa0f475921555b00-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b739d9707e819deeb987e6ae745b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T18:18:13.264Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b73b-83a1-7c6d-849e-c351c7388727","session_id":"01a1b739-d4c0-7bc3-b609-96aa963898cd","message":{"id":"01a1b73b83a17c6d849ec34ffb1a9417","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Note: old index.js `apply(ctx, config)` used `DEFAULTS` computed at import time (reads process.env at import) — that's the AC-006 problem (import side effects? reading env at import isn't output though). Design says \"导入模块时不读环境\", fixed.\n\nOld index.js did not export createPlugin/getRegistration. New does.\n\nDesign §6: `settings` 取 configPath、readonly、strict。The current implementation ignores `readonly` (doesn't even read it). Design says \"settings 取 `configPath`（缺省…）、`readonly`（缺省 false）、`strict`（缺省 false）\" — an implementation that never uses readonly is arguably fine since old code never used it either (DEFAULTS.readonly existed but unused). Hmm. To be faithful, maybe merge settings with defaults including readonly. Not tested. I'd leave it (avoid over-engineering), but a reviewer reading design may flag \"settings 取 readonly（缺省 false）\" as unmet. Hmm, \"取\" = take. It's vague. The current code takes configPath and strict. I could add a normalized settings merge for clarity:\n\n```js\nconst s = { readonly: false, ...settings }\n```\nThat's minor and harmless. But is it needed? Design §6 only describes effects of configPath and strict. I'll consider adding it to be literal, but changing code without need risks introducing inconsistency with impl.md. Let me first read impl.md to see what previous dev claimed, then decide.\n\nActually, my main deliverable now is impl.md documenting this round. Let me read impl.md (43KB - long). Let me read its beginning and structure (headings).","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"se